SUMMARY:Improv is Life!: A 4-Part Workshop
DESCRIPTION:This four-part class is ensemble-based: you're never up there a
 lone\, we learn as a group\, through games and exercises where everyone pl
 ays at once and the room shares the risk (and the laughs). Over four sessi
 ons\, you’ll go from an individual person with a fixed identity to a war
 m ball of clay: free of attachments\, form fluid\, and ready to meet each 
 moment with full use of your mental\, physical\, and vocal tools.Nothing t
 o memorize. Nothing to prepare for. Each session is a new experience. Wear
  comfortable clothing that you can move in and bring a water bottle.Improv
  is Life! is a good fit if:&nbsp\;You’ve never acted or practiced improv
  before&nbsp\;You have acted or practiced improv before\, but it’s been 
 a while&nbsp\;You currently have a robust acting and/or improv practice&nb
 sp\;You’re terrified of improv&nbsp\;You hate improvYou’re curious abo
 ut improvYou love improv&nbsp\;You’re a human who wants to have fun and 
 connect with other humans&nbsp\;Each session will start with a robust phys
 ical\, vocal\, and imaginative warm up.Session 1 - Nov 17&nbsp\;We’ll be
 gin building an ensemble with low-stakes group exercises to practice liste
 ning\, responding\, and releasing fear of failure.&nbsp\;Session 2 - Dec 1
 We’ll continue building an ensemble with simple games that invite each p
 articipant to respond authentically to unanticipated moments.&nbsp\;Sessio
 n 3 - Dec 8We’ll move into scene work using basic scripts as a foundatio
 n and building on the text with improvisational play.&nbsp\;Session 4 - De
 c 15We’ll continue partnered scene work using given circumstances as a f
 oundation and developing characterization one choice at a time.&nbsp\;Our 
 Teacher: Hannah Gould (she/they) Hannah Gould was born and raised in the B
 ay Area\, and she was shaped and seasoned by years in New York and Eastern
  Europe. Hannah is a reader\, writer\, actor\, singer\, composer\, directo
 r\, designer\, and producer. She’s a trained and experienced educator: s
 he’s taught all ages and every subject that can be used as a form of sel
 f expression.\n\nTickets & info: https://www.viewcy.com/event/improv_is_li
 fe_a_4
URL:https://www.viewcy.com/event/improv_is_life_a_4
END:VEVENT
