SUMMARY:One Year Anniversary: Olio Homecoming Dance 2026
DESCRIPTION:Our little venue is officially one year old!! And we’ve recen
 tly become obsessed with the idea of Olio running more like a public schoo
 l (all the parts we love at least). Dances\, yearbooks\, field trips\, pic
 ture day\, etc… so for our one-year anniversary party we’ve decided to
  throw a Homecoming Dance. Along those lines\, we’re excited to launch O
 lio extracurricular clubs! If you’ve had ideas about ways you want to ga
 ther with your friends/bring new people into your life through your passio
 ns but maybe have no idea where to host or need a little help spreading th
 e word\, we’re now taking submissions for monthly club ideas by members\
 , for members.&nbsp\;Pitch us one\, about anything you'd love to gather pe
 ople around. We'll pick 3 clubs to meet once a month at the Lighthouse for
  3 months\, and each club leader gets a stipend per session.Hang with your
  fellow Olio members\, dance\, smoke a cheeky cig on the roof during a cri
 sp fall night\, come back and dance and tune in for our highlight reel fro
 m the first year and what's going to be even better in year two.&nbsp\;Dre
 ss classy because the winners will be announced during the Homecoming Danc
 e.Pitch your club here. Submissions close Monday\, Oct 19.What to expect:8
 pm: Hang in the space and vote on the club ideas.9:00pm-9:30pm: Highlight 
 reel from the last year and announcement of club winners!  10:00pm - 1am: 
 DJ Zimmy Dynamite begins and plays your favorite homecoming tunes (whateve
 r that means lol)Tickets:To attend sign up for our monthly membership whic
 h gives you two credits to use towards our events each month.&nbsp\;You mu
 st be 21 or older to attend.What is Think Olio?Think Olio is an ongoing ex
 periment in lifelong learning. We are a community of open-minded people wh
 o gather to exchange ideas with new friends and connect over art\, literat
 ure\, and philosophy.An Olio is what we call the social learning events we
 ’ve been organizing since 2015. A blend between a lecture and a house pa
 rty\, Olios are led by a teacher who loves sharing their passions and the 
 room is filled with curious\, open-minded New Yorkers.&nbsp\;A year into c
 reating a venue\, one of our favorite feelings has been the moments where 
 we’ve stepped outside of time. We’ve created a space where conversatio
 ns don’t feel rushed\, people are greeted with hugs\, and as a community
 \, we spontaneously come up with new ideas (like the dial-up-disco house p
 arty) and bring them to life.Our goal is to spark new perspectives\, ignit
 e curiosity\, and enjoy ourselves socially\, an alternative to typical nig
 htlife options.Check out our full calendarDisclaimer: By purchasing a tick
 et\, you agree to have your photo/video used for social media/marketing ma
 terials. If you prefer to not have your photo taken\, feel free to send us
  a note.\n\nTickets & info: https://www.viewcy.com/event/homecoming-olio
URL:https://www.viewcy.com/event/homecoming-olio
END:VEVENT
